# Analysis contract

- @gixy/api.py is the stable entry point for embedders. Every result is
  `analysed` (issues are complete), `rejected` (Gixy could not parse the
  configuration) or `error` (the analysis did not complete). An empty `issues`
  list means "clean" only with `analysed`.
- `analyze()` must not raise for anything a configuration or its options can
  cause; new failure modes become an `error` kind, not an exception.
- `analyze()` keeps includes off by default: callers pass untrusted text.
- @gixy/cli/main.py exit codes: 0 analysed and clean, 1 analysed with issues,
  2 not analysed. Exit 2 wins when any input was not analysed.
- @gixy/formatters/json_report.py and @gixy/cli/server.py report through
  `gixy.api`; keep their `status` and error kinds in step with it. Bump
  `REPORT_VERSION` only for an incompatible change to the report object.
- `--format json` stays a bare list for existing consumers; do not add fields
  to it.
- Tests: @tests/core/test_api.py and @tests/cli/test_analysis_outcome.py.
